#!/usr/bin/env python
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
RealSense 3D Reconstruction Studio  (single-file application)
=============================================================
Intel RealSense D405 -> YOLO bottle segmentation -> RGB-D tracking (odometry + ICP)
-> pose graph -> TSDF fusion -> triangle mesh -> synchronized CAD-like inspection.

Units / conventions
-------------------
* All geometry is in METERS (export dialog can scale to millimetres).
* Scan world frame  = camera frame of the first accepted keyframe
  (RealSense convention: +X right, +Y down, +Z forward).
* Inspection/model frame = world frame rotated 180 deg about X (so +Y is up in the
  first view, +Z points toward the viewer) and translated so the mesh bounding-box
  centre is the origin. Mesh and point cloud share this frame. Exports use it.
"""
